  "notes": "Philippine reporting is heavily Taglish, so the lists mix Tagalog affixed forms with the English policy phrases the local press actually prints (executive order, price freeze, suggested retail price, state of calamity). Movement carries the infinitive/-in, completed-aspect and pag- nominal forms because headlines alternate between them. Avoided bare English single words like 'ban', 'cap' and 'permit', which fire on ordinary prose; used the multi-word phrases instead. Also dropped bare 'kalamidad' as too generic on its own."
